 How is the conditional print that never executes for n>100 speeding things up? 
 This toy code arises from a question on Math SE What is the most efficient way to determine if a natural number N can be written as the sum of two squares? . It is a surprisingly tough problem with a single thread unvectorised solution taking around 4 hours to count them out to 10 9 . 
